I'm feeling really excited, too.

181
00:12:32,080 --> 00:12:34,590
That Koyuki...He's running late!

182
00:12:34,590 --> 00:12:40,360
Ryusuke, good luck!
Bring this charm with you.

183
00:12:40,360 --> 00:12:43,200
Sorry! I stopped by the drugstore
and ran a bit late.

184
00:12:43,200 --> 00:12:45,200
I swear...

185
00:12:45,200 --> 00:12:47,200
Thank you, Granny!

186
00:12:47,200 --> 00:12:50,190
"7/29 (Thursday) 11:00"

187
00:12:57,210 --> 00:12:59,210
You can sleep too, you know.

188
00:12:59,210 --> 00:13:01,050
Yeah, I'm okay.

189
00:13:01,050 --> 00:13:07,050
It seems Saku, Koyuki, and Chiba,
couldn't sleep at all last night.

190
00:13:07,050 --> 00:13:08,210
Me too.

191
00:13:16,730 --> 00:13:17,560
Wow, that was a good nap.

192
00:13:17,560 --> 00:13:19,230
Yeah, I got some sleep too.

193
00:13:19,230 --> 00:13:21,070
What, then Taira-kun?

194
00:13:21,070 --> 00:13:23,540
I couldn't sleep yesterday, either.

195
00:13:26,070 --> 00:13:27,910
Is this where we're gonna?

196
00:13:27,910 --> 00:13:30,580
Weren't you listening at the meeting?

197
00:13:30,580 --> 00:13:34,080
This is where Belle Ame,
featuring Yoshito, will be performing.

198
00:13:34,080 --> 00:13:36,680
The main stage
accommodates 20,000 people.

199
00:13:36,680 --> 00:13:39,690
There's also a second stage,
with a 16,000 capacity,

200
00:13:39,690 --> 00:13:43,020
and the third stage
with a 12,000 capacity.

201
00:13:43,020 --> 00:13:47,190
They'll have performances
simultaneously on all three stages.

202
00:13:47,190 --> 00:13:49,680
You can walk between the stages.

203
00:13:50,700 --> 00:13:53,870
They're each about 10 minutes apart.

204
00:13:53,870 --> 00:13:55,630
Well then, let's go!

205
00:13:55,630 --> 00:13:56,660
-Yeah!
-Yeah!
-Yeah!

206
00:13:59,710 --> 00:14:03,380
Here on the second stage, hip hop artist
Malcolm will be performing.

207
00:14:03,380 --> 00:14:07,610
He's a monster of an artist who's sold
over 20 million tickets in the US.

208
00:14:07,610 --> 00:14:11,050
Well, let's head on over to the
third stage, where we'll be performing.

209
00:14:11,050 --> 00:14:13,720
Um, can we take a little break?

210
00:14:13,720 --> 00:14:15,150
It's a cute trail.

211
00:14:15,150 --> 00:14:16,020
Uh-huh.

212
00:14:18,560 --> 00:14:21,220
Don't you think our stage is kind of far?

213
00:14:26,070 --> 00:14:29,240
This is where we'll be performing...
The third stage.

214
00:14:29,240 --> 00:14:34,070
It's the smallest of the three stages,
with a 12,000 capacity.

215
00:14:34,070 --> 00:14:35,100
Hey!

216
00:14:36,510 --> 00:14:37,640
Koyuki!

217
00:14:45,020 --> 00:14:49,750
I wonder how many people will come out
to see an unknown band like us?

218
00:14:51,860 --> 00:14:56,860
Oh, I'm so hungry! I'm dying to eat!

219
00:14:56,860 --> 00:15:02,370
Here's some rice balls my mom made.
They're for everyone.

220
00:15:02,370 --> 00:15:06,870
Alright! Delicious!

221
00:15:06,870 --> 00:15:10,380
Here. Koyuki's mom made these rice balls.

222
00:15:10,380 --> 00:15:12,110
Yeah.

223
00:15:22,890 --> 00:15:27,060
Sorry...I haven't been able
to eat these past few days.

224
00:15:27,060 --> 00:15:30,430
Koyuki, Saku, sorry.
I need to go talk to him.

225
00:15:35,900 --> 00:15:41,840
These were Leon Syke's terms in exchange
for our appearance at Grateful Sound...

226
00:15:41,840 --> 00:15:45,380
He gets all royalties for
the next 5 albums we release,

227
00:15:45,380 --> 00:15:50,020
and we don't get compensated for
any tours or promotions he books us on.

228
00:15:50,020 --> 00:15:54,190
Does this mean that Leon Sykes will
be endorsing us and we'll be famous?

229
00:15:54,190 --> 00:15:59,620
Idiot! He's not going to spend
his money on an unknown band like ours.

230
00:16:01,130 --> 00:16:02,530
It's my fault.

231
00:16:02,530 --> 00:16:05,000
It's repayment for the guitar
and the dog I took.

232
00:16:06,030 --> 00:16:08,200
He's going to stick us
with a crazy schedule,

233
00:16:08,200 --> 00:16:10,870
then toss us out when we're through.

234
00:16:10,870 --> 00:16:12,540
Probably.

235
00:16:12,540 --> 00:16:15,270
But I also gave him my terms too.

236
00:16:16,710 --> 00:16:18,010
What kind of terms?

237
00:16:43,500 --> 00:16:48,200
If an unknown band like us gets
most attendance out of 3 stages...

238
00:16:50,010 --> 00:16:51,680
What're you trying to say?

239
00:16:51,680 --> 00:16:55,250
If we actually got
the most number of audience...

240
00:16:55,250 --> 00:16:57,080
would you forget everything I did?

241
00:16:59,350 --> 00:17:02,860
You think you can get a bigger audience
than these major artists?

242
00:17:02,860 --> 00:17:05,690
Would you just shut up for a second?

243
00:17:05,690 --> 00:17:08,860
Yo, you think you're in
an equal position, muthafucker?!

244
00:17:08,860 --> 00:17:11,030
I wanna take my chances.

245
00:17:11,030 --> 00:17:13,160
You...Are you serious?

246
00:17:21,870 --> 00:17:26,050
The number of people at each stage
can be counted by the staff.

247
00:17:26,050 --> 00:17:28,550
That's precious marketing material.

248
00:17:28,550 --> 00:17:30,220
Put the gun down.

249
00:17:30,220 --> 00:17:35,390
Huh?! Boss, don't,
don't listen to this muthafucker.

250
00:17:35,390 --> 00:17:40,190
Put the gun down, okay.
Goldie, this is business.

251
00:17:45,660 --> 00:17:47,190
Such a gamble...

252
00:17:48,670 --> 00:17:52,670
Hey! There's no way
we can beat out Malcolm!

253
00:17:52,670 --> 00:17:56,840
When I heard Koyuki's song...
I felt a possibility.

254
00:17:56,840 --> 00:18:00,010
Don't go betting away
our future on your hunch!

255
00:18:00,010 --> 00:18:03,180
It seems that this eve of the festival

256
00:18:03,180 --> 00:18:05,150
is going to be quite
significant for all of us...

257
00:18:06,350 --> 00:18:08,290
-Rock, paper, scissors!
-Rock, paper, scissors!

258
00:18:09,360 --> 00:18:13,160
If you can find a pastry that's not
all stale, get it for me, will ya?

259
00:18:30,710 --> 00:18:32,380
Hey, if it isn't Koyuki-kun...

260
00:18:32,380 --> 00:18:33,880
What are you doing out here?

261
00:18:33,880 --> 00:18:37,820
I-I was going to go get some eye drops.

262
00:18:37,820 --> 00:18:40,150
Are you staying at the campsite?

263
00:18:40,150 --> 00:18:42,650
Uh-huh. What about you?

264
00:18:42,650 --> 00:18:45,210
Koyuki-kun, can you come with me awhile?

265
00:18:46,490 --> 00:18:50,000
I wonder which stage Maho will go see...

266
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:54,170
If Maho comes to see my stage,

267
00:18:54,170 --> 00:18:58,170
then you give up on her
and never show your face again.

268
00:18:58,170 --> 00:19:02,010
And if I agreed to that,
will you do the same?

269
00:19:02,010 --> 00:19:03,340
You bet.

270
00:19:03,340 --> 00:19:06,350
Good. I wanted to clear things up too.

271
00:19:06,350 --> 00:19:08,410
I guess this will settle things then.

272
00:19:08,410 --> 00:19:09,240
Yeah.

273
00:19:15,520 --> 00:19:18,520
The Performance Eve Festival
has a jam session,

274
00:19:18,520 --> 00:19:21,590
a copying contest and all kinds of fun.

275
00:19:21,590 --> 00:19:25,360
Hmm. Would have been nice to participate.

276
00:19:25,360 --> 00:19:29,870
Hey you guys!
What are you guys doing there?!

277
00:19:29,870 --> 00:19:31,700
Oh, Aunty...

278
00:19:31,700 --> 00:19:33,870
Picking my nose.

279
00:19:33,870 --> 00:19:38,310
We were told that an audition band
like ours couldn't participate.

280
00:19:38,310 --> 00:19:41,310
Who told you such nonsense?!

281
00:19:41,310 --> 00:19:43,650
Ah, those were Ran-san's orders...

282
00:19:43,650 --> 00:19:44,820
What?!

283
00:19:44,820 --> 00:19:46,490
Fine. You boys come with me.

284
00:19:46,490 --> 00:19:49,820
We can go in? Wow, Aunty,
you've got some clout here!

285
00:19:49,820 --> 00:19:50,820
I told you!

286
00:19:50,820 --> 00:19:53,420
It was my sister who originally
put together Grateful Sound.

287
00:19:57,160 --> 00:19:58,990
If Maho...

288
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:00,990
Hey!

289
00:20:03,000 --> 00:20:04,000
Dude, over here!

290
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:05,770
Huh, me?

291
00:20:05,770 --> 00:20:08,340
Dude, I finally found you!

292
00:20:08,340 --> 00:20:10,540
Yeah, the guy in the movie, alright!

293
00:20:12,080 --> 00:20:14,010
He's...he's a small kid, man!

294
00:20:14,010 --> 00:20:15,180
He is small!

295
00:20:15,180 --> 00:20:19,690
Uh...eh...uh...
You guys are from Kneecap...

296
00:20:19,690 --> 00:20:21,850
Kneecap? Right.

297
00:20:21,850 --> 00:20:24,690
We're trying to play a Crush song
on the eve of the festival.

298
00:20:24,690 --> 00:20:26,780
Would you play with us, if you like?

299
00:20:27,860 --> 00:20:31,200
I...can't...English...

300
00:20:31,200 --> 00:20:32,560
Yo!

301
00:20:32,560 --> 00:20:34,200
Yoshito-kun?

302
00:20:34,200 --> 00:20:36,390
Want me to translate for you?

303
00:20:39,970 --> 00:20:41,910
Where the heck did Koyuki go?

304
00:20:41,910 --> 00:20:44,400
I wonder if he couldn't
find any pastries...

305
00:20:50,320 --> 00:20:51,320
Who's that kid?

306
00:20:51,320 --> 00:20:53,820
-Hey, isn't that the boy
in the Dying Breed movie?
-Huh?! That's him?

307
00:20:53,820 --> 00:20:55,320
-What was the name of their band?
-Mongo-Mongolian something?

308
00:20:55,320 --> 00:20:58,450
No way! He's such a little kid!
I'm bummed!

309
00:20:59,830 --> 00:21:04,330
Come on, Koyuki. I'm counting on you.
These people here are the core fans...

310
00:21:04,330 --> 00:21:06,170
If you can make an impact here tonight,

311
00:21:06,170 --> 00:21:08,360
they may follow us to our stage tomorrow...

312
00:21:09,500 --> 00:21:13,840
Beck's fate depends on you!

313
00:21:13,840 --> 00:21:15,400
Ooh! It's the Crush!

314
00:21:23,680 --> 00:21:25,170
I don't know this song.

315
00:21:30,690 --> 00:21:33,020
Thanks for the translation...

316
00:21:36,200 --> 00:21:38,160
Get off the stage!

317
00:21:38,860 --> 00:21:41,200
What did you say?? Damn you!

318
00:21:41,200 --> 00:21:43,370
Please do not throw things on to the stage!

319
00:21:43,370 --> 00:21:46,430
You there with the black cap,
please calm down!

320
00:21:53,050 --> 00:21:57,820
It was quite a while after
the festival that Saku told me.

321
00:21:57,820 --> 00:22:02,690
Later that night, Ryusuke defeated
his former bandmate Eiji.

322
00:22:16,240 --> 00:22:18,740
Yo! I got the pastries.

323
00:22:18,740 --> 00:22:20,070
Tomorrow's forecast?

324
00:22:20,070 --> 00:22:24,010
It's supposed to be sunny. With maybe
a few showers in the afternoon.

325
00:22:26,580 --> 00:22:27,740
I see...

326
00:22:29,410 --> 00:22:32,580
Let's eat some pastries together!

327
00:22:32,580 --> 00:22:34,920
It's not stale?

328
00:22:34,920 --> 00:22:36,690
Nah.

329
00:22:36,690 --> 00:22:38,690
Saku...

330
00:22:38,690 --> 00:22:39,750
Yeah.

331
00:22:43,460 --> 00:22:48,830
Full moon sways

332
00:22:50,300 --> 00:22:56,300
Gently in the night of one fine day

333
00:22:56,300 --> 00:22:59,010
What a fool

334
00:22:59,010 --> 00:23:02,480
I don't know 'bout tomorrow

335
00:23:02,480 --> 00:23:07,320
What it's like to be

336
00:23:07,320 --> 00:23:09,310
Ah...

337
00:23:10,480 --> 00:23:12,320
I was fool

338
00:23:12,320 --> 00:23:16,490
Couldn't let myself to go

339
00:23:16,490 --> 00:23:21,260
Even though I feel

340
00:23:21,260 --> 00:23:27,170
The end

341
00:23:46,120 --> 00:23:51,650
Full moon sways

342
00:23:52,960 --> 00:23:59,990
Smiling in my arms for all those years

343
00:24:13,750 --> 00:24:17,590
Last time, when I dove into
the audience, I fell on my head...

344
00:24:17,590 --> 00:24:18,820
But I didn't get hurt!

345
00:24:18,820 --> 00:24:19,680
A-ho!
